            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>These pink- and peach-furred fey resemble large bipedal meerkats. They often wear simple clothes and bands of gemstones wrapped with string and leather. These gems are elegantly cut in the shapes of lizards, scorpions, and desert blooms. Grit flingers possess an innate ability for controlling sand and carry a magical sack of endless sand they use to augment their talents. They tend to live in small communities with expansive tunnel networks deep below ground, typically beneath deserts and badlands.</p>\n<p>These resilient fey are believed to guard deposits of precious materials, such as of gemstones, silver, and the purest of iron. The easiest way to anger a grit flinger is to dig near their homes. Upon discovering a hole or tunnel, they'll use their endless sandy sack to fill it in. They then summon a giant sandstorm to scare off any remaining creatures, transforming the landscape into a desert as a warning for any who might think of excavating there.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Feybound"
            }
